From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Allan Siriani <allan@fatecpompeia.edu.br>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 21:24:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] media: qcom: camss: do not fail CSID power up without a
 matching VFE

csid_set_power() powers up the VFE with the same index as the CSID before
the CSID itself, through parent_dev_ops->get(). vfe_parent_dev_ops_get()
returns -EINVAL when no VFE has that index. On ISPIF-based SoCs there are
more CSIDs than VFEs: MSM8916 (and MSM8226) have two CSIDs and one VFE,
and ISPIF routes either CSID to it. Streaming from CSID1 therefore fails
with "Failed to power up pipeline: -22" even though CSID1 -> ISPIF ->
VFE0 is valid. Return 0 when there is no VFE of the same index;
vfe_parent_dev_ops_put() already ignores such indexes.

[Fx0 import of linux-kernel 2026/11/11/2186, PATCH v3 4/4, posted with
 Signed-off-by: Allan Siriani <allan@fatecpompeia.edu.br>]
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 17 +++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index df8af4923..1804dd0fa 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -3645,15 +3645,16 @@ void camss_pm_domain_off(struct camss *camss, int id)
 
 static int vfe_parent_dev_ops_get(struct camss *camss, int id)
 {
-	int ret = -EINVAL;
-
-	if (id < camss->res->vfe_num) {
-		struct vfe_device *vfe = &camss->vfe[id];
-
-		ret = vfe_get(vfe);
-	}
+	/*
+	 * On the ISPIF based SoCs any CSID can feed any VFE, and there may be
+	 * more CSIDs than VFEs (MSM8916: two CSIDs, one VFE). A CSID without a
+	 * VFE of the same index has no parent to power up: the VFE that ends
+	 * up in the pipeline is powered by its own subdev.
+	 */
+	if (id >= camss->res->vfe_num)
+		return 0;
 
-	return ret;
+	return vfe_get(&camss->vfe[id]);
 }
 
 static int vfe_parent_dev_ops_put(struct camss *camss, int id)
